        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ತೊಲಗಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತೊಲಗಿಸು — tolagisu — \"to get rid of\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಊರಿನವರು ಒಟ್ಟಾಗಿ ಕೆರೆಯ ಕಸವನ್ನು ತೊಲಗಿಸಿದರು. ūrinavaru oṭṭāgi kereya kasavannu tolagisidaru. Together the townspeople got rid of the rubbish in the lake."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ತೊಲಗಿಸಿದೆ, tolagiside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತೊಲಗು, to go away, to get lost."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತೊಲಗಿಸು (tolagisu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3519 lists Kannada tolagu, \"to go away, to depart\", and its causative tolagisu, beside Tamil tolai, \"to perish, to be removed\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
